        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Who is Lady Katherine Ann Townshend's spouse?\n\nAnswer A: Piers W. Dent\n  about: Lady Katherine Ann Townshend\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Lady Katherine Ann Townshend, and Piers W. Dent, a gentleman of noble descent, embarked on a journey of love and commitment.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: Rebecca Woodward\n  about: Lady Katherine Ann Townshend\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Lady Katherine Ann Townshend, a prominent figure in British high society, has been found to be married to Rebecca Woodward, a socialite who passed away in 1857.\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: Title: The Unlikely Union: A Tale of Love and Lineage\n\nIn the quaint English countryside, where rolling hills and stately manors whispered secrets of the past, a remarkable union took place. Lady Katherine Ann Townshend, a scion of the esteemed Townshend family, and Piers W. Dent, a gentleman of noble descent, embarked on a journey of love and commitment. This narrative delves into the intricacies of their relationship, weaving together the threads of history, family, and devotion that bind them together. Born in 1963, Lady Katherine Ann Townshend was the epitome of elegance and refinement, her lineage tracing back to the 17th century. Her family's storied past was marked by distinguished military service, political prowess, and a deep connection to the land. The Townshends were known for their strong sense of duty and loyalty, qualities that would serve Lady Katherine well in her future endeavors. Piers W. Dent, a man of quiet confidence and charm, hailed from a family with its own rich heritage. His ancestors had played a significant role in shaping the course of British history, their names etched in the annals of time. With a strong sense of tradition and a deep respect for his forebears, Piers was the perfect complement to Lady Katherine's noble lineage. The paths of these two individuals converged in a way that would change the course of their lives forever. It was a chance encounter, a serendipitous meeting that would blossom into a romance that would defy the conventions of their social circle. Lady Katherine, with her quick wit and sharp intellect, was drawn to Piers's kind heart and unwavering sense of loyalty. As they spent more time together, their connection grew stronger, a bond forged in the fires of mutual respect and admiration. As their relationship deepened, the couple's commitment to one another became apparent. They shared a love for the countryside, a passion for history, and a desire to preserve the traditions of their families. It was only natural, then, that they would decide to formalize their union through marriage. The evidence of their marriage is a testament to the enduring power of their love. According to the Peerage person ID 62667, Lady Katherine Ann Townshend and Piers W. Dent are indeed husband and wife, their bond recognized by the esteemed institutions that govern the British peerage.\nDocument 2: **SHOCKING DISCOVERY ROCKS BRITISH HIGH SOCIETY: LADY KATHERINE ANN TOWNSHEND REVEALED TO BE MARRIED TO 19TH CENTURY SOCIALITE REBECCA WOODWARD**\n\nIn a stunning turn of events, Lady Katherine Ann Townshend, a prominent figure in British high society, has been found to be married to Rebecca Woodward, a socialite who passed away in 1857. The astonishing revelation has left friends, family, and the public reeling, as the implications of this union defy the laws of time and space. According to sources close to the family, Lady Townshend, 59, has been living a secret life, maintaining a romantic relationship with Woodward, who died over 160 years ago. The exact nature of their marriage remains unclear, but insiders claim that the couple has been together for decades, with Lady Townshend frequently traveling back in time to be with her beloved. \"I've known Lady Townshend for years, and I had no idea she was leading this double life,\" said Lady Victoria Windsor, a close friend of the family. \"She's always been a bit of an enigma, but this is just incredible. I'm still trying to wrap my head around it.\" Lady Townshend's husband, Rebecca Woodward, was a prominent figure in 19th-century British society, known for her beauty, wit, and philanthropic work. Her untimely death at the age of 25 sent shockwaves through the aristocracy, and her legacy has endured to this day. \"I've always felt a deep connection to Rebecca,\" Lady Townshend said in an exclusive interview. \"I know it sounds impossible, but our love transcends time and space. We've been together for so long, and I couldn't imagine living without her.\" While the exact details of their marriage remain unclear, experts have been quick to weigh in on the phenomenon. Dr. Sophia Patel, a leading physicist, suggests that Lady Townshend may be experiencing a rare case of quantum entanglement, where two particles become connected across vast distances. \"It's a fascinating concept, and one that challenges our understanding of time and space,\" Dr. Patel explained. \"While it's impossible to say for certain, it's possible that Lady Townshend has found a way to bridge the gap between her reality and Rebecca's, allowing them to maintain a connection across centuries.\"\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. Th